# Task: list regular files under a directory that are at least a given size.
# Program: this file.
# Run: execute docs/recipes/server-large-files.program --input directory=/var/log
#      execute docs/recipes/server-large-files.program --input directory=/srv --input min_size=+1G
# Test with fakes: create a temporary directory with one 2 MB file and one small file, then
#   run with min_size=+1M and expect only the large file.
# Explain: the output is find's own list of paths, one per line.
# Replaces (Bash): find "$1" -type f -size "+100M" -print
accept directory as text
accept min_size as text with default "+100M"
run "find" with arguments [directory, "-type", "f", "-size", min_size, "-print"]
